      },
      {
        "id": "t016",
        "text": "01 Physical Layer (L1): The foundation of all transit. It encompasses the raw transmission of bits over physical media including copper wires, fiber optics, or radio waves.",
        "region_id": "r005",
        "role": "正文"
      },
      {
        "id": "t017",
        "text": "02 Network Layer (L3): Responsible for packet forwarding and routing. It utilizes logical IP addresses to find paths across multiple network nodes.",
        "region_id": "r005",
        "role": "正文"
      },
      {
        "id": "t018",
        "text": "03 Transport Layer (L4): Manages end-to-end communication. TCP provides reliable delivery via handshakes, whereas UDP prioritizes speed over integrity.",
        "region_id": "r005",
        "role": "正文"
      },
      {
        "id": "t019",
        "text": "04 Application (L7): The interface for users. HTTP for web browsing, SMTP for mail, and SSH for secure remote management operate here.",
        "region_id": "r005",
        "role": "正文"
